available sizes: Small 148cm, Medium 151cm, Large 154cm
sizing note: Size down 6-10cm from what you normally ride
board type: All Mountain
flex: Stiff
rider level: Intermediate - Advanced
shape: Tapered Directional
camber type: Directional Extra Camber (predominantly positive camber with subtle rocker in nose)
sidecut type: Tapered Bi-Radial Sidecut (underfoot width of a wide board while maintaining tip/tail width)
width: Standard
mounting pattern: 2x4 Inserts
topsheet: Topless Topsheet (graphics transferred directly to fiberglass, reduces weight and material usage)
laminate: Carbon Infused Glass, Carbon Array 5, Double Impact Plates
carbon details: 90° carbon fibers woven into glass for added pop and response
carbon array 5: Five carbon stringers in binding zone for power distribution and board control
impact protection: Double Impact Plates (two layer urethane weaves beneath each binding area for compressive strength)
core: Performance Core (blend of high-strength Aspen and Bamboo wood)
sidewall: Carbon Slimewalls (carbon and Slimewall material from inserts to contact points for pop, stability, responsiveness)
base: Sintered, Stone Ground Race Base (carbon-infused sintered base for maximum speed)
edges: Cleave Edge Steel (nearly 50% more steel for resistance to cracking, can be detuned to larger radii)
tip/tail construction: Thin Con (tapered tips and tails to reduce swing weight, improve tip flex, boost durability)
resin: Bio Resin (plant-based epoxy from renewable resources like vegetable oils)
terrain: All Mountain (aggressive riding, big mountain, high speed)
related model: Warpig (Superpig is souped up version of Warpig)
